WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.230
My name is Erik Verlinde.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:06.970
I work on emergent gravity, and I'm trying
to explain the phenomena associated to dark

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:08.740
matter.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.690
Emergent gravity is a way of describing gravity
which explains where gravity comes from by

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:21.039
thinking about space-time as being built out
of microscopic quantum information.

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:25.710
This quantum information is entangled and
from thinking about the entanglement entropy

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:31.590
we can derive Newton's Law and the Einstein
equations.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.860
But now in the case of our universe, we also
have dark energy.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:41.640
And what I show is that from dark energy you
can actually explain, using emergent gravity,

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:48.800
what happens in galaxies like galaxy rotation
curves that start flattening, which are normally

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.370
explained through dark matter.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:57.210
Now dark matter is thought of as a particle,
but in my theory there is no particle of dark

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.210
matter.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:04.239
Dark matter is just a phenomena that emerges
from the way that gravity works in our universe.

